  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC) Country Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TradeMark Africa&apos;s DRC Country Programme works to unlock the trade potential of Africa&apos;s second-largest country by tackling the structural bottlenecks that constrain both formal and informal trade, particularly in Eastern DRC. Operating along the Northern, Central, Lobito, and Kribi-Zongo corridors, the Programme invests in physical trade infrastructure, including One Stop Border Post upgrades at Mahagi and Ruzizi II and port modernisation at Kalundu and Kasenyi on Lake Tanganyika, while advancing digital customs systems such as ASYCUDA World and the Single Electronic Window (SEGUCE) to cut clearance times and reduce opportunities for corruption. Complementing these hard and digital infrastructure interventions, the Programme supports alignment of DRC&apos;s trade policy with AfCFTA and EAC protocols, strengthens quality standards and sanitary and phytosanitary systems, and runs targeted initiatives, including the Women in Trade Programme to transition informal traders, particularly women in Goma and Bukavu, into formal trade channels and connect them to regional markets.</narrative>
  </description>
